{
  "schema": "chipmunk.contextual-token-short-email-transfer/1",
  "methods": {
    "unit": "Complete exact decoded EML sentence of at least 12 segmenter words; current context joins previous, focus and next sentences by spaces.",
    "training": "Fit on six previously consumed short email groups. A known rewritten sentence is positive; unchanged sentences, original files and genuine human-replacement files are negative. Standardize columns and fit L2 C=.5 logistic with balanced source weights per class.",
    "calibration": "Different four previously consumed groups. In each, take the largest human response across both files. Strictly exceed highest (zero reference-group flags) or second highest (at most one reference-group flag). These are empirical review cutoffs, not probabilities or rate guarantees.",
    "arms": "Current raw three-sentence support; separately calibrated existing window odds versus contextual focus token margins with the same fitting method; compare native window and focus score AUC plus paired localization.",
    "scope": "Reuse the native encoder and its linear classification head. Use token positions to reduce logits for exact focus codepoints; exclude special tokens and require complete non-whitespace coverage. Verify the average over all actual attention-valid token logits reconstructs native logits. Context still informs every focus hidden state, so this is not independent word authorship evidence.",
    "measure": "Any positive highlight, human variant/source flags, missed edits, wrong location and useful edit at non-whitespace IoU at least .30. All groups and thresholds frozen before fresh model outcomes."
  },
